flowchart TB
  accTitle: Inference generation lifecycle
  accDescr: The current generation serves queries during candidate preparation, backfill, catchup, indexing, and verification. Cutover switches the active pointer to the verified candidate and retains the previous generation. Rollback switches the pointer back only if the previous generation is eligible. Retirement is a separate destructive operation, allowed only for inactive generations that are no longer eligible rollback targets.
  subgraph build[Candidate build: current generation keeps serving queries]
    direction LR
    prepare["Prepare<br/>storage and capture"] --> backfill["Backfill<br/>boundary snapshot"]
    backfill --> catchup["Catchup<br/>source changes"]
    catchup --> index["Index<br/>vector index"]
    index --> verify["Verify<br/>required checks"]
  end
  subgraph pointers[Activation and cleanup are separate decisions]
    direction LR
    cutover["Cutover<br/>switch active pointer"] --> active["New active<br/>previous retained"]
    active -. rollback if eligible .-> restored["Previous active<br/>new retained"]
    active -. separate decision .-> retire["Retire inactive generation<br/>no eligible rollback dependency<br/>destructive"]
    restored -. separate decision .-> retire
  end
  build --> pointers
  class verify,cutover decision
  class active,restored active
  class retire destructive
